 d move with their children to a remote village in Norway\, hoping to rebui
 ld their lives near Lisbeth's family. There\, they grow close to their nei
 ghbors\, the Halbergs\, whose warmth gives them hope for a fresh start. Bu
 t the fragile peace begins to unravel when the Gheorghiu family’s young 
 daughter\, Elia\, arrives at school covered in bruises.\nhttps://www.thetr
 iplex.org/movie/fjord\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/wes
 ternma/
